# Job: Core tests — interface-based tests link the shared library; implementation tests become unit tests; LTO test build time fixed

You are a codex sub-agent under a Claude supervisor. Model gpt-6-astra, reasoning xhigh. Cap 3.5 h. Work ONLY in the detached worktree `/home/hep7/project/zlink-core-tests` (already checked out at main; run `git -C /home/hep7/project/zlink-core-tests status` first). Never touch `/home/hep7/project/zlink`. Do not commit; leave the diff in the worktree and write `git diff` (plus new files via `git add -N`) to `/tmp/zlink-core-tests/fix.patch`. Never modify `doc/spec/**` (report needed spec/CONTRIBUTING sentences instead). Read `core/tests/README.md`, `core/tests/TEST_REFACTOR_POLICY_SPEC.md`, `core/CONTRIBUTING.ko.md` §5, and `AGENTS.md` §2/§3/§5. Campaign rules: no coverage loss, no assertion weakening, one rule per concern, fewer rules.

## Problem (supervisor-verified)
`core/tests/CMakeLists.txt:293` links every test through `testutil-static` → `libzlink-static`, and `core/CMakeLists.txt:122-132` enables `CMAKE_INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION` for non-Debug builds. Result: each of the 123 integration test executables (plus 28 unittests and the C test) performs a full LTO link of the whole Core — the Release+LTO gate build (`core/build-gate`, `-DBUILD_TESTS=ON`) is dominated by test linking. `core/tests/testutil.hpp:9-13` includes internal headers (`src/runtime/platform.hpp`, `internal_defs.hpp`, `utils/fd.hpp`), and 7 integration tests include `src/` headers directly: `test_flow_state_c_api.cpp`, `monitoring/test_monitor_enhanced.cpp`, `test_dealer_router_single_lane_contract.cpp`, `test_helper_recv_part_basic.cpp`, `test_flow_state_paired.cpp`, `test_phase3_request_reply_contract.cpp`, `test_multi_socket_contract_regressions.cpp`.

## Rule to establish (user decision)
Tests are interface-based. **Integration/contract/e2e tests use only the public C API (`core/include/zlink.h` family) and link the shared `libzlink` exactly like a user** — no internal headers, no private symbols, no LTO relink per executable. **Tests of internal data structures are unit tests** under `core/tests/unittest/`, linked against Core objects; they must not be built as LTO links per executable either.

## Task
1. Measure first: in the worktree configure `core/build-gate` as the gate does (`cmake -S core -B core/build-gate -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DBUILD_TESTS=ON -DWITH_TLS=ON -DBUILD_BENCHMARKS=ON`) and record wall time of a clean `cmake --build core/build-gate -j8` split into library vs tests (e.g. `--target libzlink` then the rest), and the size of `.ninja_log`/make timing per test link. Keep the numbers for the report.
2. `testutil*`: remove the internal includes; whatever they were used for (fd helpers, platform macros) gets a public-API or test-local equivalent. Make `testutil` link `libzlink` (shared). Integration tests link `testutil` + shared `libzlink` (rpath to the build lib dir; Windows PATH property as the C test already does).
3. The 7 offenders: split each into (a) the public-API contract part that stays in integration and (b) the internal-structure assertions that move to a new/extended `unittest_*.cpp`. If an internal assertion only re-verifies what a public observation already proves, drop it and say so per assertion (coverage stays by the public test). List every moved/dropped assertion in the report.
4. Unit tests: link Core objects without a per-executable LTO link — e.g. a single non-LTO `OBJECT`/static target for tests (`INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION OFF` on the test object library, `-ffat-lto-objects` is not acceptable as the general fix), or one `unittest` executable aggregating all unit test sources with one link. Choose the option with the fewest rules and explain the alternative you rejected.
5. Keep ctest labels/lanes (`integration;serial`, `unittest`, `hotpath_gate`), `run_test_lanes.sh`, the Windows/MSVC branches, ASAN/TSAN/UBSAN presets coherent. `hotpath_gate` and `core/tests/perf/hotpath_reference.json` untouched.
6. Verify in the worktree: clean Release+LTO gate build (report before/after wall times), `ctest` all lanes via `bash core/tests/run_test_lanes.sh --build-dir core/build-gate` (0 failures), `ctest -R '^hotpath_gate$'` PASS within ±5%, a Debug configure+build (`core/build-dev` equivalent in the worktree, `scripts/build-core.sh` may hard-code paths — replicate its flags) to make sure tests still build there, and `nm -D` / `ldd` proof that integration tests use only exported `zlink_*` symbols and the shared library.

